#
#	thumb-specific files
#
#	What is hand written here is what the compiler has no word for on
#	an ARMv7-M core: the exclusive monitor, SDIV and UDIV, the long
#	multiply, and the floating point control word.  The rest is the
#	portable C, which is correct and slow, and that is the right order
#	to do it in.
#
#	The 386 and portable files are named rather than thumb ones
#	because they are the little-endian versions.  The Thumb files this
#	directory used to carry were for a big-endian ARM with an FPA, and
#	neither of those is an ARMv7-M core.
#
TARGFILES=\
	ainc-thumb.$O\
	div-thumb.$O\
	getfcr-thumb.$O\
	vlop-thumb.$O\
	vlrt-arm.$O\
	frexp-386.$O\
	nan-386.$O\
	memmove.$O\
	memset.$O\
	strchr.$O\
